{
  "dom_id": "step-39080",
  "name": "The Significance of Bayes' Theorem",
  "problem": "Bayes' theorem states that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/e1d65c5f59724230a371e63ff62bb8796d63bcb12e31ca7ff2b18bca00e3ba99.svg)\n\nFor reasons that will become clear shortly, we'll rewrite Bayes' theorem in a slightly different (but equivalent) form:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/ed7bfbd78af1660b10856f6a78b66c8596b0b1dd0ade839bc910a6381475b98a.svg)\n\nBayes' theorem is significant because it lets us update our belief that a hypothesis is true when new evidence emerges. For this reason, it has numerous applications in science, computer science, and engineering.\n\nFor example, suppose a doctor wishes to assess the probability that a certain patient is infected with a particular disease. It is known that those aged ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/1f1a501ced780d95ba1f0d886e696028662607bb0b37b13f9d7d3a1d1db60185.svg) or older are observed to have a higher probability of carrying the disease.\n\nLet's define the events ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/7533ad047439b7d799dd7afee5d6a7bc9f4404fbadb8c3f27ef6d3952119ff6b.svg) as follows:\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/9df014bbe82f5fd83bfb40f253da072a3873355ea7f25a2199a25f1385f0d171.svg) the event that a randomly selected patient has the disease\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/3ba12d975885bf1e318d35e51e6977174296f53bc4172ee24b458fcf0ea282a5.svg) the event that a randomly selected patient is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/1f1a501ced780d95ba1f0d886e696028662607bb0b37b13f9d7d3a1d1db60185.svg) years old or more\n\nThen, Bayes' theorem gives the following:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/26685b6a61d42e30e594cd99e0715abecd393aba35468887a6149dbf3305d9f0.svg)\n\nLet's introduce some new terminology:\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/078062d17441bd681fcb9f3b8358e22f3c6460a2f25027a9379ee3e9f822cf97.svg) is called the **prior.** It tells us the probability that a randomly selected patient has the disease *without considering any other factors*.\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/8d07649dab5e4db06b27ee2c94bec75806ab4b8facf9f0994bcd482b0e4eff21.svg) is called the **posterior**. It tells us the probability that a randomly selected patient has the disease *taking into consideration* that they are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/1f1a501ced780d95ba1f0d886e696028662607bb0b37b13f9d7d3a1d1db60185.svg) or older.\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/a76e4b2e92fa0c3f3c0afed43f96387cbdd7db6f6e5fb915eb1f1d1807bfc927.svg) is called the **likelihood.** It tells us the proportion of infected people that are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/1f1a501ced780d95ba1f0d886e696028662607bb0b37b13f9d7d3a1d1db60185.svg) or older. This quantity could be estimated by taking a random sample from the population of infected people and computing the ratio of those who are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/1f1a501ced780d95ba1f0d886e696028662607bb0b37b13f9d7d3a1d1db60185.svg) or older.\n\nTherefore, Bayes' theorem lets us update the hypothesis (the patient has the disease) by incorporating information about the patient (they are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/1f1a501ced780d95ba1f0d886e696028662607bb0b37b13f9d7d3a1d1db60185.svg) or older) and available evidence (an estimate of the proportion of infected people who are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14211553/assets/1f1a501ced780d95ba1f0d886e696028662607bb0b37b13f9d7d3a1d1db60185.svg) or older). \n\nFurthermore, suppose the likelihood is updated at a later date (e.g., due to more evidence being available as more people become infected). In that case, this will further improve the accuracy of the posterior when future patients are assessed.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-39080\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"39080\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"6468\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-39080\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-5\">The Significance of Bayes' Theorem</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"39080\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <p>Bayes' theorem states that\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" display=\"true\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -2.172ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24.802ex\" height=\"5.475ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1460 10962.6 2420\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><path data-c=\"1D443\" d=\"M287 628Q287 635 230 637Q206 637 199 638T192 648Q192 649 194 659Q200 679 203 681T397 683Q587 682 600 680Q664 669 707 631T751 530Q751 453 685 389Q616 321 507 303Q500 302 402 301H307L277 182Q247 66 247 59Q247 55 248 54T255 50T272 48T305 46H336Q342 37 342 35Q342 19 335 5Q330 0 319 0Q316 0 282 1T182 2Q120 2 87 2T51 1Q33 1 33 11Q33 13 36 25Q40 41 44 43T67 46Q94 46 127 49Q141 52 146 61Q149 65 218 339T287 628ZM645 554Q645 567 643 575T634 597T609 619T560 635Q553 636 480 637Q463 637 445 637T416 636T404 636Q391 635 386 627Q384 621 367 550T332 412T314 344Q314 342 395 342H407H430Q542 342 590 392Q617 419 631 471T645 554Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(751,0)\"><path data-c=\"28\" d=\"M94 250Q94 319 104 381T127 488T164 576T202 643T244 695T277 729T302 750H315H319Q333 750 333 741Q333 738 316 720T275 667T226 581T184 443T167 250T184 58T225 -81T274 -167T316 -220T333 -241Q333 -250 318 -250H315H302L274 -226Q180 -141 137 -14T94 250Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1140,0)\"><path data-c=\"1D434\" d=\"M208 74Q208 50 254 46Q272 46 272 35Q27